}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0.5 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0860eddb-8872-5a14-90cd-ea80f80450d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469656} {:answer/id #uuid "a9503884-f719-56eb-b3d2-1bbf12f445b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9503884-f719-56eb-b3d2-1bbf12f445b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469657} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ceb7b39-d9d7-59a0-905c-bc078aea9c08" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0316227b-bc46-5340-873c-fb4bdb297900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469658} {:answer/id #uuid "73b30d62-76b6-5783-bbcb-a165c097c0d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0316227b-bc46-5340-873c-fb4bdb297900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :a